-- an automorphism of a molecule: a relabelling of its atoms, with the relabelling that undoes it,
-- preserving every atom's element and every pair's bond. The inverse is carried as data rather than
-- asserted, so the group structure below is written without any further principle; this is the
-- object chemistry's canonicalizers compute (color refinement, Morgan 1965 at CAS) and then throw
-- away, keeping only one of the numberings it relates.
Auto : Mol → Type 0
Auto M = (f : mol-atoms M → mol-atoms M)
       × (g : mol-atoms M → mol-atoms M)
       × ((x : mol-atoms M) → g (f x) ≡ x)
       × ((x : mol-atoms M) → f (g x) ≡ x)
       × ((x : mol-atoms M) → mol-el M (f x) ≡ mol-el M x)
       × ((x : mol-atoms M) → (y : mol-atoms M) → mol-bd M (f x) (f y) ≡ mol-bd M x y)
